## Item 1 — SUB special case (`review-campaign-dotnet.md` row `4644af9d03`: REVERT)
`ZLinkBackendSocketPoller.cs:19-38,65-99` branches SUB sockets to `ZlinkPoll.Poll` instead of the public `IPoller` because the .NET binding's `Poller.Add` used to claim a completion owner even for sockets that did not request `PollCompletion`. The binding now acquires the owner only when `PollCompletion` is requested (`bindings/dotnet/src/Zlink/Runtime/Eventing/Poller.cs:39-58`, worklog D-074). First pin that binding behaviour with a framework contract test (register a SUB with POLLIN only on the public poller alongside a completion-owning DEALER; both progress); then delete the SUB branch so every socket uses the ordinary `IPoller` POLLIN path (spec `core/doc/spec/core/05-polling.ko.md` §3-4). Run the fanout/subscriber test classes.

